  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 255 AM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nAbove-normal temperatures and dry conditions are expected next \nweek as the westerlies retreat northward with a strengthening low-\nlevel thermal ridge and the return to southerly winds. \n\nTemperature spread among bias-corrected probabilistic guidance \nremains minimal, with even the 10th percentile indicating warm, \nabove-normal temperatures through the end of the week. Both \ndeterministic and ensemble guidance point to an elongated mid- \nlevel ridge (~585-587 dam) as the primary influence of the weather\nacross the Southern Plains. High temperatures toward the end of \nthe week are forecast to climb toward or even exceed 90 deg F. \n\nMahale",
